  "reputation": {
    "summary": "SMD-only, so not a socket-rolling legend, but liked as a cheap, rugged all-rounder. A diyAudio member called it 'a 21st century version of the NE5532'. Builders value 36 V operation, rail-to-rail high-drive output and short-circuit protection for direct headphone drive. Forums suggest it as an SMD OPA2604AP substitute. No ASR or Samuel Groner measurements known.",
    "sonic_descriptors": [
      "very good all-rounder",
      "21st-century NE5532"
    ],
    "typical_uses": [
      "Headphone output stage (reportedly Topping NX4 DSD; DIY amps)",
      "Line buffers, converters and headphone pre-amps (synth DIY)",
      "DAC reconstruction filters; DJ-mixer cue outputs",
      "SMD substitute for OPA2604 / OPA2134 in new designs",
      "Retro-computer and sound-card audio (ZX-Evolution, Mac NuBus PAS16)"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "8 nV/√Hz is modest versus OPA1656 (2.9 nV/√Hz), OPA1612 or OPA1602; not ideal for phono or mic.",
      "SMD only (SOIC-8, WSON-8; quad SOIC-14, VQFN-16). Rolling needs an adapter; WSON is hard to adapt.",
      "Limited drive for low-impedance headphones: short of a 250 mW / 18 Ω target; NX4 modders swapped in INA1620.",
      "Little independent measurement; praise rests mostly on specs and value.",
      "TI's 'next-generation OPA2134/OPA2604 replacement' FAQ concerns OPA1656, not OPA1688."
    ],
